# 🌦 Weather Monitoring Station – Project Journal

> **Project Duration:** 18 Hours  
> **Platform:** Arduino Uno  
> **Project Type:** Hardware Project

---

# 📖 Introduction

I built this Weather Monitoring Station to learn how Arduino works with sensors. The project measures the surrounding temperature and humidity using a DHT11 sensor and displays the readings on a 16×2 I2C LCD display.

I divided the project into three parts. In the first part, I completed the hardware setup. In the second part, I programmed the Arduino and tested the sensor. In the final part, I completed testing, organized the circuit, and prepared the documentation.

---

# 🎯 Objectives

- Learn how the DHT11 sensor works.
- Read temperature and humidity using Arduino.
- Display sensor values on an LCD.
- Improve hardware assembly skills.
- Gain experience in Arduino programming.

---

# 🛠 Activities Performed

### Part 1 – Hardware Setup (6 Hours)

- Collected all required components.
- Learned about the DHT11 sensor and LCD module.
- Connected the Arduino, sensor, and LCD.
- Checked every wire carefully.
- Verified the hardware setup before programming.

---

### Part 2 – Programming & Testing (6 Hours)

- Installed the required Arduino libraries.
- Wrote the Arduino program.
- Uploaded the code successfully.
- Displayed temperature and humidity on the LCD.
- Tested the project several times and fixed small wiring issues.

---

### Part 3 – Final Testing & Documentation (6 Hours)

- Organized the jumper wires neatly.
- Tested the project for a longer time.
- Observed stable sensor readings.
- Captured project photographs.
- Prepared the README, circuit diagram, wiring diagram, flowchart, BOM, and other project files.

---

# ⚠ Challenges Faced

- Understanding the correct sensor connections.
- Loose jumper wire during testing.
- Selecting the correct COM port before uploading the code.
- Adjusting the LCD display properly.
- Arranging the wiring neatly.

---

